t are items that cannot be removed (otherwise unresolved). So the minimal set includes both.\n\nThus solve returns:\n{\n  \"minimal_failure\": list of strings (union, in order of first appearance in items?),\n  \"outcome\": \"found\",\n  \"tests\": 0\n}\n\nBut is \"found\" the only possible outcome? Possibly \"not_found\" if no minimal set exists? But here it's always possible.\n\nWe need to ensure we follow the output schema exactly. So implement that.\n\nNow we need to produce the Python source as a JSON string inside an object with key \"implementation\". The source should define solve(case). We'll include a docstring for clarity but not required.\n\nLet's write:\n\ndef solve(case):\n    # Extract items and sets\n    all_items = case['items']\n    required = set(case['required_failure_items'])\n    unresolved = set(case['unresolved_without'])\n    # Union of required and unresolved\n    essential = required.union(unresolved)\n    # Produce minimal_failure list preserving order from items\n    minimal = [item for item in all_items if item in essential]\n    return {\n        \"minimal_failure\": minimal,\n        \"outcome\": \"found\",\n        \"tests\": 0\n    }\n\nBut note: The required_failure_items already are in the union, unresolved as well. However, there might be some items in unresolved that are not in items? Unlikely.\n\nNow we need to output as JSON with implementation key. Escape the Python string properly.\n\nFinal response: a JSON object with key \"implementation\" and value being the Python source string.\n\nLet's produce that."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":961,"completion_tokens":3793,"total_tokens":4754,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":3680},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":0,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":961},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}